BIDeT  --  big text and terminal art, drawn as SIXEL graphics

Created and maintained by
    Chris Pollitt   <chris.pollitt@gmail.com>

BIDeT 4D (the BIF format, the tools bifin, bifop, bifout and bidet, the 3D and
animation stage, the presets, the tests and the documents) was developed with
pair-programming assistance from Claude (Anthropic).  See the "Co-Authored-By:"
trailers in the git history for details.

Borrowed from, with thanks.  Nothing below is bundled in this repository unless
it says so:

    css3wordart   --   https://github.com/arizzitano/css3wordart
        The WordArt preset designs (colours, gradient stops, side colours,
        camera tilts) that BIDeT3D renders in 3D, and that the materials of
        BIDeT 4D (rainbow, chrome, gold, superhero ...) are re-expressed from.
        Data only, no code copied.  The repository has no licence file, so its
        Word textures are NOT bundled (3D/get-textures.sh fetches them).

    libsixel      --   https://github.com/saitoha/libsixel   (MIT)
        Used by BIDeT3D (legacy) to encode SIXEL.  BIDeT 4D writes SIXEL
        itself and does not need it.

    Pillow and numpy
        The only libraries BIDeT 4D needs.  Not bundled.

    banner(1), FIGlet and TOIlet
        banner: AT&T, UNIX System V.  FIGlet: Glenn Chappell and Ian Chai.
        TOIlet: Sam Hocevar.  The eras of the time machine ("bidet --time-
        machine").  The real programs are used if they are installed, and
        imitations drawn from a font if not.  Nothing of theirs is bundled.

    TrueType fonts
        None are bundled.  BIDeT finds the ones your system has.  The tests
        write a tiny font of their own (tests/ttfbuild.py).

Developed and tested mostly in mintty, on Cygwin, with Python 3.8 to 3.12 under
Windows, WSL and Cygwin.  See the Terminals note in 4D/README.md.

A great many cows were harmed in the making of this program.  They were
extruded, turned, and popped out of the screen, and they seemed to enjoy it.
